==English==
===Etymology===
{{wikipedia}}

Mistranslation of "君達の基地は、全てCATSがいただいた (in original context: ''we (CATS) have taken all of your bases'')." 

This grammatically incorrect "[[w:Engrish|Engrish]]" phrase originated in the English subtitles to the game [[w:Zero Wing|Zero Wing]] and became a [[catch phrase]] and a phenomenon.

===Phrase===
{{infl|en|phrase|head[[all]] [[your]] [[base]] [[are]] [[belong]] [[to]] [[us]]}}
#{{context|Internet|jocular}} Generally used to [[tout]] [[victory]] over an opponent, or simply to be amusing.

